Name: wtl
URL: https://sourceforge.net/projects/wtl/
Version: 9.1 (build 5321)
License: Microsoft Public License (Ms-PL)
License File: Ms-PL.txt
Security Critical: yes

Local Modifications:
None. The headers are byte-for-byte upstream apart from line endings, which
are LF here to match .gitattributes.

That is worth recording, because the WTL 8.0 copy this replaced carried five
sets of changes and every one of them has since landed upstream:

  * The licence header. WTL 8.0 shipped under CPL 1.0 and the vendored copy
    had the Ms-PL header pasted over it; 9.1 is Ms-PL upstream.

  * min and max replaced with __min and __max, which was patch #1871358 on
    SourceForge: with NOMINMAX defined before windows.h, min and max do not
    exist, while __min and __max always do. WTL 9.1 uses the underscored forms
    throughout and has no bare min( or max( call left.

  * C4302, 'type cast': truncation from LPCTSTR to WORD, in atldlgs.h and
    atlmisc.h. _U_STRINGorID::m_lpstr holds either a string or an
    INTRESOURCE -- a small integer in a pointer -- and these sites want the
    integer; casting a pointer straight to WORD is ill-formed on Win64. The
    local fix was (WORD)(ULONG_PTR); 9.1 uses LOWORD(), which is the same
    thing in the spelling the SDK uses.

  * C4706, assignment used as a condition, in atlgdi.h's AtlGetDibBitmap. The
    local fix parenthesised the assignment. 9.1 lifts it out of the condition
    altogether, and while it was there also bounded the memcpy that follows --
    so upstream fixed more than the warning.

  * An ATL11 guard in atlapp.h, so the DLL version helpers are declared when
    _ATL_VER >= 0x0B00, which modern ATL removed from atlbase.h. This one was
    never a local invention: it is 9.1's text verbatim, comment included, and
    had been back-ported to keep WTL 8.0 building with Visual Studio 2022.

Two headers are new in 9.1 and were not in the 8.0 set: atldwm.h (Desktop
Window Manager) and atlribbon.h (Ribbon UI). Nothing here includes them. They
are kept so this is the complete upstream Include directory rather than a
subset nobody chose deliberately -- a missing header is a confusing failure,
and an unused one costs nothing.
